  "prediction": "INLINE JUMP-CACHE PROBE (lane.ibcache, #507, commit 27554f7145, merged onto master as a6ec5ec0ab). At the lookup_and_goto_ptr site of the x86 front end (gen_eob, DISAS_JUMP) the TB emits tb_lookup()s hit test as TCG IR: it reads cpu->tb_jmp_cache with the same hash and compares the same key (pc, cs_base, flags, cflags) read at run time; a hit does goto_ptr to the cached TB, a miss calls the unchanged helper_lookup_tb_ptr. It changes how the next TB is found, never which TB runs, and it inherits every jump-cache invalidation (a wiped slot is empty, a discarded TB carries CF_INVALID). ARMS: A = master 4e3d69a69b, B = a6ec5ec0ab (A plus the probe, default on). The full pgraph sweep. REGISTERED LEGS: every capture must_not_move, bit-identical; better = 0, worse = 0. UNCOMFORTABLE OUTCOMES NAMED NOW: (1) any capture moving, better or worse, means the probe ran a TB the helper would not have (a stale slot, a key field read wrongly) and kills the change as written until found; (2) an arm that hangs or crashes on a suite is the same finding; (3) a capture not byte-identical with itself within an arm is noise and not attributed.",
